From: nomorecoolnicknames <nomorecoolnicknames@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 17:38:45 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] FMRadio: the activity honours the short antenna too

FmMainActivity kept its own headset-only isAntennaAvailable(), so with
ro.mtk_fm_short_antenna_support the service powered the tuner up while
the UI still asked to connect headphones.
---
 src/com/android/fmradio/FmMainActivity.java | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/com/android/fmradio/FmMainActivity.java b/src/com/android/fmradio/FmMainActivity.java
index 82db51b..216a23a 100644
--- a/src/com/android/fmradio/FmMainActivity.java
+++ b/src/com/android/fmradio/FmMainActivity.java
@@ -852,7 +852,10 @@ public class FmMainActivity extends Activity implements FmFavoriteEditDialog.Edi
      * @return true or false indicate antenna available or not
      */
     private boolean isAntennaAvailable() {
-        return mAudioManager.isWiredHeadsetOn();
+        // Same rule as FmService.isAntennaAvailable().
+        return mAudioManager.isWiredHeadsetOn()
+                || android.os.SystemProperties.getBoolean(
+                        "ro.mtk_fm_short_antenna_support", false);
     }
 
     /**
